--
--
N5008 [temp.deduct.call]/4 (derived-to-base deduction).  Deducing a
class-template base `impl<I, H, T...>` from an argument of a class derived from a
specialization of `impl` now works, including when (a) the derived class is a
plain non-template `struct D : impl<...>` and (b) the trailing parameter pack `T`
deduces to a non-empty pack.  CBMC previously aborted when the argument type was
not itself a template instantiation, before the derived-to-base dispatch could
run; fixed by walking the argument class's bases for a specialization of the
deduced template.  This is the mechanism behind std::get<I> on std::tuple.
Non-vacuous: f<0> and f<1> deduce different elements of the matched base.
